STRUCTURAL CONCLUSION
  Taking U = the whole period makes the boundary term vanish, so the cut condition reads N(sqrt32 - 1/rho) <= 0, i.e.
  rho <= 1/sqrt32: the Kepler bound itself.
  The cut condition is therefore EQUIVALENT to Kepler for periodic packings, not an independent analytic inequality, and a search finding no counterexample is vacuous rather than weak evidence.
  Both FCC and HCP are exact equality cases (b = 0 for every cell), so they cannot discriminate; the icosahedral-cluster fixture has b > 0 on its central cell but a mean cell volume far ABOVE sqrt32, so its full-period sum is negative and it does not refute.

